{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he was not.</b> The daughters thought that the sons of those who gathered against YHWH would not inherit." "<b>For he died in his sin.</b> Rabbi Judah Halevi the Spaniard said that the phrase כי בחטאו מת (for he died in his sin) is joined with ובנים לא היו לו (and he had no sons), just as one says today, 'because of his sins such-and-such happened to so-and-so' — and it is not far-fetched."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:36.813116074Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}